id: pm-brief-q325
title: Surface governance findings in agent briefs via sdk/governance
description: "Adopt the pm-cli sdk/governance scanners (findDuplicateClusters, scanStaleInProgressItems, scanStorageIntegrity, scanMutationSecrets) in the brief to surface duplicate clusters, stale in-progress work, storage integrity problems, and committed secrets — token-budget-aware with actionable pm remediation commands and a governance-only mode."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T11:57:51.360Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T14:16:59.984Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T12:20:04.220Z"
author: pi-agent
resolution: Integrated sdk/governance scanners into token-budgeted briefs and hardened the PR against static-analysis and latest-CLI integration failures.
expected_result: "Agent briefs surface safe, actionable duplicate, stale-work, storage-integrity, and secret findings without leaking secret values."
actual_result: All four governance signal classes render with remediation commands; fail-isolated concurrent scans and safe custom-field handling are verified by real latest-CLI workspaces and the 137-test release gate.
notes[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T11:57:57.785Z",pi-agent,"SDK export surface confirmed: 31 exports from sdk/governance (findDuplicateClusters, scanStaleInProgressItems, scanStorageIntegrity, scanMutationSecrets, projectValidateCounts, runValidate, etc.). scanMutationSecrets(payload) returns SecretGuardFinding[] with rule + path only — secret value never returned. Verified: scanMutationSecrets({description:'AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE...'}) => [{rule:'aws_access_key',path:'$.description'}]."
  "2026-07-26T11:58:01.518Z",pi-agent,"findDuplicateClusters({pmRoot,threshold}) does a single metadata-read batch sweep — better than the per-candidate findSimilarItems loop the existing 'brief duplicates' command uses. scanStaleInProgressItems(pmRoot, items, {threshold_hours}) reads history for last_activity_at. scanStorageIntegrity needs typeToFolder from resolveItemTypeRegistry(readSettings(pmRoot)). ItemMetadata type exported from @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk — must map PmItem to ItemMetadata (required fields: id,title,description,type,status,priority,tags,created_at,updated_at)."
  "2026-07-26T12:20:03.575Z",claude,"Verified by orchestrator (claude): typecheck OK, 135/135 tests, build OK. Functional proof in a throwaway workspace seeded to trigger each finding — two exact-title items, one in_progress task, one item carrying a fake AWS key. 'pm brief' emitted a Governance section with: duplicate cluster (score 1, exact_title) plus the resolving command 'pm update br-nop2 --dep id=br-15gy,kind=related'; and a secrets finding reporting item id + field + detector name (aws_access_key) with the secret VALUE correctly withheld, plus a redaction command. Stale scan correctly reported nothing (the in_progress item was seconds old)."
  "2026-07-26T13:52:04.224Z",codex,"Review hardening on PR #44: fixed all five DeepScan defects, replaced explicit any with SDK CommandHandlerContext/ExtensionApi/FlagDefinition types, removed dynamic imports, and made real-workspace E2E tests hermetically use the project-local pm CLI 2026.7.26 while accepting both documented create JSON envelopes. release:check passes 135/135 tests with zero production vulnerabilities; measured source coverage remains 82.84% lines, 74.67% branches, 92.19% functions and is tracked separately rather than claimed as complete."
  "2026-07-26T14:13:07.674Z",codex,"Final CodeRabbit review found 11 actionable hardening items. Implemented fail-isolated concurrent governance scans, safe inspect-only remediation for unsupported secret paths, complete oldest-item duplicate remediation, sound governance narrowing, Slack/markdown fixes, non-vacuous tests, cwd-safe E2E, and operational cost documentation. Large-tracker benchmark: 481 items, 1.48s elapsed, 137 MB peak RSS on pm CLI 2026.7.26."
  "2026-07-26T14:16:59.968Z",codex,"Post-review release evidence: NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null npm run release:check passes typecheck, build, 137/137 tests, zero production vulnerabilities, npm pack dry-run, and pm-changelog verification."
files[3]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,Governance collection and rendering
  test/brief.test.ts,project,Unit and real-workspace integration coverage
  README.md,project,Default governance scan cost and opt-out guidance
tests[1]{command,path,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  "NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null npm run release:check",test/brief.test.ts,project,1800
close_reason: "Shipped: sdk/governance findings (duplicate clusters, stale work, storage integrity, secret scan) surfaced in the brief within the token budget, each with the exact pm command that resolves it. Verified functionally end-to-end."
